# The Go API, reachable only from the Next.js server. The browser never gets
# this address: it talks to Next.js, and Next.js talks to Go, which is what
# lets the API run with no public listener of its own.
#
# It is read server-side only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, deliberately), and
# every lib/ module and route handler reaches it through lib/serverFetch.ts,
# which also attaches the viewer's session token as an Authorization: Bearer
# header. Defaults to http://localhost:8080 when unset.
API_URL=http://localhost:8080
